# O'Pip Feature Bus SHADOW evidence capture
# Dedicated, bounded, non-overlapping evidence producer for the R4-B2 shadow
# comparator path. This is NOT the protected unified cycle: it runs as its own
# process on the one scheduler (cron) and never takes the unified-cycle lock, so
# it cannot delay or skip a protection cycle.
#
# Cadence: every 15 minutes. The capture is authorized only when
# OPIP_FEATURE_BUS_MODE=shadow AND OPIP_CANONICAL_WRITER_MODE=shadow; otherwise it
# is an inert recorded no-op.
#
# Bounds (derived, not arbitrary):
#   * internal total wall-clock budget: OPIP_FEATURE_BUS_CAPTURE_BUDGET_SECONDS
#     (default 180s; capped at 220 so budget + one 20s reservation <= the 240s
#     timeout below, keeping the internal budget the graceful stop).
#   * per-request reservation: 20s (Kraken client request timeout is 15s + slack)
#   * max requests per pass: capture limit (8) + universe refresh (2) ~= 10
#   * worst-case request time ~= 10 * 20s = 200s; the internal budget stops the
#     pass once the remaining budget cannot fit one more bounded request, and the
#     outer timeout below is final containment only.
#   * outer timeout 240s < the 900s cadence, so two passes cannot overlap; flock
#     adds explicit non-overlap safety.
#   * 240s is independent of, and never contends with, the 60s unified cycle.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

*/15 * * * * root flock -n /var/run/opip-feature-bus-capture.lock -c 'cd /opt/OHM-Trade-Agent-v1/OHM-Trade-Agent-v1 && timeout --signal=TERM --kill-after=20s 240 /usr/bin/docker compose exec -T ohm-trade-agent python -m app.jobs.capture_feature_bus_shadow >> /var/log/opip-feature-bus-capture.log 2>&1'
